{"t": 1205.578, "n": 252, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "The code step is finished. All six plan rows are marked with `✓ 2026-11-25`, the plan's status is `completed`, and the code report is written. The one `tempergraph self-check` run printed PASS, and the full suite, `ruff check src tests` and `mypy` all ran with exit code 0. I changed no file after it.\n\n- **Phase 1, the pytest plugin:**\n  - `tempergraph.pytest_plugin` sets `TEMPERGRAPH_HOME` to a per-test folder and `TEMPERGRAPH_LOOP` to `off` through `monkeypatch`. A test that sets the loop itself afterwards keeps its value.\n  - The engine's `pyproject.toml` declares it under the `pytest11` entry point.\n  - New tests in `tests/test_suite_isolation.py` start a scratch package with no conftest, from its own folder and from another folder.\n  - A control run with the plugin blocked does change the seeded home, so the real-home check can fail.\n  - Before the plugin existed, four of the five new tests failed. The spec-text test passed already because discovery had written the specs.\n- **Phase 2, `stats forget [--check]`:**\n  - The new `observe/forget.py` and a change to `cli/observe_cli.py` remove gone state roots from the machine index. They also remove their rows from this month's run and session stats, except rows an outbox still lists.\n  - The verb prints each removed root with its row count. With `--check` it changes no file. Without `--check` it exits 2 saying the index is in use if it can't get the index lock in 2 s.\n  - `tests/test_central_stats_forget.py` has 8 tests, which failed first with `invalid choice: 'forget'` and then passed.\n\nDeviations, all in `docs/tasks/i144.report.md`:\n- I wrote each phase's marks as three edits of the plan instead of one.\n- `forget` returns early without taking the lock when no index entry is gone.\n- The scratch-package helper sets `PYTHONUSERBASE` so a seeded `HOME` doesn't hide installed packages.\n\nARTIFACT code_report: docs/tasks/i144.report.md\nARTI